libmpeg2 0.5.1 as mpegv.library builds it
==========================================

This directory is libmpeg2 0.5.1 (GPL-2.0-or-later; COPYING, AUTHORS),
from https://github.com/cisco-open-source/libmpeg2: its C decoder only
(libmpeg2/*.c and their headers; not the MMX, AltiVec, Alpha, VIS or ARM
files, nor libmpeg2convert, libvo or the programs). It was added to
mpegv.library unchanged (git: "third_party/libmpeg2: libmpeg2 0.5.1,
unchanged"); these are mpegv.library's changes since, each marked
"mpegv:" where it is made. They are GPL-3.0-or-later, (c) 2026 Brian
King, as mpegv.library is (its LICENSE).

The build has no configure script: mpegv.library's src/config.h says what
the 68k (and the build machine, for the tests) is.

Changes that alter no picture (14 November 2026)
-------------------------------------------------

- libmpeg2/alloc.c: its memory from mpegv.library's mpv_malloc and
  mpv_free (exec's AllocVec on the Amiga), not the C library's.

- libmpeg2/decode.c: the chunk buffer 256 KB, not 1194 KB. It holds one
  slice (or header) at a time; a DVD's largest whole picture (MP@ML's
  buffer) is 229 KB. A megabyte less a decoder.

- include/mpeg2.h, libmpeg2/header.c: mpeg2_sequence_t keeps the
  sequence header's aspect ratio and frame rate codes as stored
  (aspect_code, rate_code), for mpegv's MpvGetInfo.

The IDCT made quicker, the same to the bit (14 November 2026)
-------------------------------------------------------------

- libmpeg2/idct.c: mpegv_idct_copy and mpegv_idct_add, chosen by
  mpeg2_idct_init in place of libmpeg2's C (which stays, and is what
  MPEGV_PLAIN builds). The same rows, columns, sums and shifts; only what
  a block needs is done: zero rows passed over, DC-only rows filled, rows
  with only the four lower frequencies (or only MPEG-2's mismatch
  coefficient) with fewer products; the columns from the rows used only
  (row 0 alone, rows 0/1/4/5, those and row 7, or all), clipped straight
  into the picture; a DC-only block as one value; the products MULS.W
  (16 bits by 16) on a 68k, each butterfly as its four products.
  tests/idct_test.c checks it against libmpeg2's C on random blocks of
  every kind (and on a 68020 under vamos), and libmpeg2's IEEE 1180
  accuracy.
